**Challenge:** 

The password for the next level is stored in the only human-readable file in the inhere directory. 
Tip: if your terminal is messed up, try the “reset” command.

**Solution & Explanation:****
```
STEP 1: ls         
# list files and folders in the home directory

STEP 2: cd inhere      
# navigates into inhere directory

STEP 3: ls
# check what files/directories can visibly be seen in the inhere directory
# 10 files are shown. All beginning with the name -file followed by a double digit number sequence
starting from 00 and ending at 09 (-file00, -file01, -file02, etc.)

STEP 4: cat -- "-file*" OR cat ./-file*
# either one of these commands will display all of the contents of all of the files all at once
# lots of computer junk is being displayed along side the password so it is difficult to discern what the password could be 

STEP 5: file -- *
# checks all the contents of every single file and displays info of each file's content type
# since our files all begin with - we use -- to disable the option feature so as to not make it confused
# -file07 is the only file with ASCII text which is considered a human-readable file

STEP 6: cat -- "-file07" 
        cat -- -file07 
        cat ./-file07

# these are the different commands that will display the contents of the file


