**What I learned:** 

the file commmand is a command that checks inside a file and does not care 
about the name but rather cares about the content.

file → asks Linux what type a file is (text, picture, program, junk, etc.)

* → means all files in this folder

ASCII text = clean words and numbers

data = computer junk
